                    "number": 7,
                    "title": "CONCLUSION",
                    "text": [
                        "1. Optimal repeater insertion ($k = 8$, $h = 1.775$) reduced simulated delay from $3.0005\\text{ ns}$ to $1.0349\\text{ ns}$ (65.51% reduction), comparing well with the theoretical delay of $0.8911\\text{ ns}$.",
                        "2. Cascaded driver ($k_{casc} = 3$) yielded $3.0961\\text{ ns}$ (theoretical $1.8152\\text{ ns}$), proving that distributed repeaters are far superior to lumped drivers for long distributed $RC$ interconnects."
                    ]
